    "Description": "The perl-HTTP-Daemon package includes the HTTP::Daemon class, a subclass of IO::Socket::IP. Instances of the HTTP::Daemon class are HTTP/1.1 servers that listen on a socket for incoming requests.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* perl-HTTP-Daemon: HTTP::Daemon: Arbitrary code execution via OS command injection in send_file() (CVE-2026-8450)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
